radeontop(1)
============
Lauri Kasanen
:doctype: manpage
:man source: RadeonTop
:man version: 1.4
:man manual: RadeonTop Manual
:revdate: 2026-08-09

NAME
----
radeontop - report Radeon GPU utilization

SYNOPSIS
--------

*radeontop [-cThmv] [--dither-seed 'seed'] [-b 'bus'] [-d 'file'] [-i 'seconds'] [-l 'limit'] [-p 'device'] [-t 'ticks']*

DESCRIPTION
-----------
RadeonTop samples Radeon engine-status registers and reports total GPU activity
plus the hardware blocks whose status bits have an exposed gauge.

R600 and later use `GRBM_STATUS` through a radeon or amdgpu DRM interface when
available. R300-class integrated graphics (RS400, RS480, RS482, and RS485) use
`RBBM_STATUS` through PCI `resource2`; detection selects the direct path when
the radeon read-register ioctl rejects the pre-R600 register.

Every dump invocation emits one `radeontop_capture_v1` JSON header. It carries
one clean source commit, the exact source and build manifests plus their
digests, boot and device identity, and the byte-escaped command vector. Dump
mode rejects dirty and unknown source identities because they lack an immutable
source object. Each data line retains its human-readable fields and ends with
an `evidence_v2` JSON object containing the run identity, timing, slot
accounting, capability and signal state, clock means, lane denominators, and
unconditional missing-data bounds. A
`radeontop_run_end_v2` footer records the logical exit reason, last observed
committed generation, and typed device, clock, or schedule terminal cause.

OPTIONS
-------
*-b, --bus 'bus'*::
	Select one hexadecimal PCI bus number from 00 through ff. For the lspci
	address `01:00.0`, the bus argument is `1`.

*-c, --color*::
	Enable colorized output.

*-d, --dump 'file'*::
	Append dump records to 'file'. An argument equal to `-` writes stdout;
	other names, including names beginning with `-`, name regular files. Each
	invocation appends a new provenance header. A regular destination, including
	redirected stdout, carries an exclusive lock for the whole run. A nonempty
	regular destination receives a newline record boundary before the new header,
	so a truncated prior record cannot absorb the run identity. Runtime
	diagnostics use stderr. `SIGTERM` and `SIGINT` request an orderly footer,
	flush, and shutdown.

*--dither-seed 'seed'*::
	Offset each sample reproducibly inside its own exact slot using a seed from
	0 through 4294967295, default 7919. Rejection sampling gives every
	nanosecond in the slot equal probability, and a fixed seed reproduces a run
	exactly. A seed of 0 selects the exact deadline grid instead.
+
Dithering carries the default because the exact grid aliases against a workload
whose period lands near one sample slot, meeting the same phase of every cycle
and reporting that phase as the whole duty. The exact grid is the better
sampler where it oversamples the workload period, and worse where it aliases.
Dithering costs a few percent of nominal slots to scheduler lateness near the
end of a slot, which every window reports through *cov*.

*-h, --help*::
	Display help on stdout and exit successfully.

*-i, --dump-interval 'seconds'*::
	Publish one dump window every 'seconds'. The accepted range is 1 through
	86400 and the default is 1.

*-l, --limit 'limit'*::
	Stop after 'limit' data lines in dump mode. Zero, the default, runs until
	termination.

*-m, --mem*::
	Force the direct PCI sysfs `resourceN` MMIO path selected by the known
	device family. An unknown PCI ID has no admitted direct layout. With
	--path, this option forces MMIO for the same selected PCI device.

*-p, --path 'device'*::
	Open the named DRM device node and derive its exact PCI identity. The path
	selects the device instead of --bus; --mem can still force the validated
	direct status path for that same device.

*-t, --ticks 'ticks'*::
	Request 'ticks' samples per second from 1 through 1000000. The default
	rate is 120. A higher rate increases temporal resolution and overhead;
	scheduler lateness and register-read cost can reduce the valid sample
	count. The duty figures stay truthful at whatever rate the sampler
	reaches, because each divides by the reads that validated, so 'cov'
	carries the shortfall and 'readshare' attributes it: the fraction of the
	window the device reads occupied. A small share beside a low coverage
	puts the cause on the wake-up path rather than on the register read.
	'meanread' and 'maxread' answer different questions, because a tail read
	moves the maximum by two orders and leaves the mean where it was.

*-T, --transparency*::
	Enable terminal transparency.

*-v, --version*::
	Display the source version and exit successfully.

INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
--------------------
*C, c*::
	Toggle colorized output.

*Q, q*::
	Quit.

